    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and all 3 tests pass with a full green build.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented an optional, region-validated `postcode` field for owners, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions.\n\n**Validation logic (single responsibility, reused existing code):**\n- `util/RegionPostcodes.java` \u2014 new pinned region\u2192range table (NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099) with `allows(region, postcode)`; a region with no known range is permissive. Mirrors the existing `CityRegion` util rather than duplicating city knowledge.\n- `rest/function/owner/ValidatePostcode.java` \u2014 a small step that validates **only when present**: requires 4 digits, then derives the region via the existing `CityRegion.of(city)` and checks the range via `RegionPostcodes.allows(...)`. Missing/blank postcode is accepted, keeping the contract backward-compatible.\n- `escalation/InvalidPostcodeException.java` + `InvalidPostcodeExceptionHandler.java` + escalation YAML \u2014 a checked exception handled as 400, matching the existing single-field-error pattern (`InvalidTelephoneLengthException`).\n\n**Storage & return:**\n- Added `postcode` to `OwnerFields` in `openapi.yml` (flows into the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto`), and a `postcode` column/field on the `Owner` entity \u2014 so MapStruct maps it both ways automatically (no mapper change). Added the column to all four `schema.sql` files (existing inserts use explicit column lists, so seed data is unaffected).\n- `ApplyOwner` now also copies postcode, so PUT updates persist it.\n\n**Wiring:**\n- Inserted a `validatePostcode` step into `owners.POST.yml` (after required-field validation) and the `owners/{ownerId}.PUT.yml` pipeline (after body validation, before load) \u2014 so an invalid postcode is a 400 regardless of endpoint.\n\nAll three acceptance tests (`coreStoresValidPostcode`, `coreAcceptsOwnerWithoutPostcode`, `errorRejectsMalformedPostcode`) and the full suite pass \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
